  "intro": [
    {
      "title": "Four forms to move with",
      "title_pl": "Cztery formy ruchu",
      "body": "You know the do / z phrases. Now four ready-made forms to build real sentences with — take them as chunks, the full verbs come later:\n\nIdę do... = I'm going to...\nIdziesz do...? = are you going to...?\nWracam z... = I'm coming back from...\nWracasz z...? = are you coming back from...?",
      "body_pl": "Cztery gotowe formy: Idę / Idziesz (do...), Wracam / Wracasz (z...). Całe czasowniki później.",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Chunk",
          "English",
          "Example"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Idę do...",
            "I'm going to...",
            "Idę do sklepu."
          ],
          [
            "Idziesz do...?",
            "are you going to...?",
            "Idziesz do szkoły?"
          ],
          [
            "Wracam z...",
            "I'm coming back from...",
            "Wracam z miasta."
          ],
          [
            "Wracasz z...?",
            "are you coming back from...?",
            "Wracasz ze szkoły?"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Questions by tone",
      "title_pl": "Pytanie tonem",
      "body": "Idziesz do sklepu? is already a question — just the tone rises. Czy idziesz do sklepu? is the same question with czy in front. Both are correct; both are accepted here.",
      "body_pl": "Idziesz do sklepu? = pytanie tonem. Czy idziesz do sklepu? = to samo z czy.",
